{
  "title": "Let users override shopping list item categories (and persist \
corrections)",
  "description": "Categories are computed server-side at response time \
(server/src/api/shopping_list/list.rs, sync.rs call \
ingredient_categorizer::categorize) and never stored. There is no way for a \
user to fix a miscategorized item, and corrections have nowhere to go.\n\
\n\
Add a persisted per-item category override:\n\
- DB: nullable category column (or override column) on shopping_list_items via \
migration.\n\
- API: allow setting/clearing it in UpdateShoppingListItemRequest and the sync \
endpoint; when set, it wins over the computed category in responses.\n\
- UI: recategorize affordance on BOTH web \
(ramekin-ui/src/pages/ShoppingListPage.tsx) and iOS \
(ramekin-ios/Ramekin/ShoppingListView.swift + ShoppingListMutationSupport/sync \
path).\n\
- End-to-end tests for the new API behavior before wiring up the UIs (per repo \
policy).\n\
\n\
Besides the UX fix, the stored overrides become a permanent labeled-data \
feedback loop for improving data/ingredients.json (see \
p2-shopping-list-category-golden-set-from-prod).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
